  "query_preview": "..\nActive weather continues for the long term as low pressure \ncontinues to remain in the Gulf for the start of the weekend. With\nthe low staying in place, some onshore flow will continue \nallowing for moisture to remain across the area. Guidance today \nhas moved away from the idea of the remnants of Typhoon Koguma \nimpacting the panhandle for the weekend. Instead, GEFS and EPS are\npointing towards the low moving into British Columbia. The main \nlow that has been affecting the panhandle will still be in the \narea bringing increased winds across the southern panhandle. \nMoving into the start of next week, guidance still has some good \ndivergence on model outputs but conditions could remain somewhat \nactive although there is a chance we see a break in the weather \nbefore another low looks to potentially move into the western Gulf\nby Monday evening.",
